test_libraries.py,myenv/Lib/site-packages/_pyinstaller_hooks_contrib/tests/test_libraries.py,ab1a87725d1c6b431f769a4717baf896d5cce3ce,KPaccarizi/PacMan,https://api.github.com/repositories/789530524/contents/myenv/Lib/site-packages/_pyinstaller_hooks_contrib/tests/test_libraries.py?ref=cf70c78eaeebae92583ccfee8f8613c9557d4503,https://api.github.com/repositories/789530524/git/blobs/ab1a87725d1c6b431f769a4717baf896d5cce3ce,https://github.com/KPaccarizi/PacMan/blob/cf70c78eaeebae92583ccfee8f8613c9557d4503/myenv/Lib/site-packages/_pyinstaller_hooks_contrib/tests/test_libraries.py,Recreating the PacMan game. This is a PacMan game that we will make it more advanced for fun,,0,1,6,25,2024-08-29T10:26:55Z,3,1,"# PacMan

Pacman is a simple game written on Pygame. The game was created as a learning project to explore the possibilities of Pygame and develop game applications.


📝 About The Project
For those of you not familiar with Pacman, it's a game where Pacman moves around in a maze and tries to eat as many food pellets as possible, while avoiding the ghosts. If Pacman eats all the food in a maze, it wins.


## Getting Started

Follow these instructions to get a copy of the project up and running on your local machine for development and testing purposes.

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.x
- Pygame library

![PacMan](pacman.png)


### Create and Activate a Virtual Environment

python -m venv myenv
myenv\Scripts\activate  # On Windows
source myenv/bin/activate  # On macOS/Linux
Install Dependencies

### Make sure you have the required dependencies installed:
pip install pygame
Running the Game

